          {
            "id": "s1:p2",
            "text": "Galium glaucum or waxy bedstraw is a plant species of the Rubiaceae. It is native to central Europe from Portugal to Ukraine, and sparingly naturalized in a few locations in North America (Quebec, Ontario, Connecticut and New Jersey)."
          },
          {
            "id": "s1:p3",
            "text": "Subspecies\nThree subspecies are recognized:"
          },
          {
            "id": "s1:p4",
            "text": "Galium glaucum subsp. australe Franco - Spain and Portugal\nGalium glaucum subsp. glaucum - France to Ukraine\nGalium glaucum subsp. murcicum (Boiss. & Reut.) O.Bolòs & Vigo - southeastern Spain"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
